  "reason": "The best result so far is config_002 (rna_only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) at 0.591 acc, showing that multiprofile + avgpool is the strongest RNA configuration. The key remaining uncertainty for the RNA pathway is whether a learned nonlinear encoder (scvi_n200) can outperform the linear PCA baseline. Config_005 isolates exactly this variable—changing only the RNA encoder from pca_n2000 to scvi_n200 while holding profile (multiprofile) and aggregation (avgpool) fixed—giving a clean comparison against config_002. This is the highest-value next step because: (1) RNA dominates over image (0.485 vs 0.208), so improving the RNA representation is the most impactful lever; (2) if scvi improves on PCA, it establishes a stronger backbone before exploring multimodal fusion; (3) if it does not, PCA is confirmed as sufficient and we can redirect remaining budget toward fusion or image-encoder questions. With 5 experiments left after this one, resolving the encoder question now prevents wasted budget on multimodal configs built on a suboptimal RNA representation."
}

